A modern newrly built community center with landscaping architecture where provided multiple service; Bayview Legal Clinic, Children care, Hangry cafe, and many more:

- A huge area for people who prefer to work in a quite place with free wi-fi and dedicated workplaces;
- Hanger cafe provides unique delicious meal for affordable prices; - Access center with comuters and educational options;
- Next door Children Center for a harmonic child development;
- Perfectly organized Free Legal Clinic where people bring their  questions and share them with qualified attorneys - vollunteers;
- A big parking with the EV charger station is located behaind the building (entrance from Davidson&Evans);
- Right accross the MUNI buses and T-line train station (Evans street).
- A very unique the environmental architecture (Stongetown) at front of this building which have an organized a picnic place with open grills (but there are no tents nor covers which will be very inconvenient while the weather is  sunny or windy) and walking routes.  If you want to celebrate your own event (wedding, B-day, graduation, etc.) call this center in advance for a possible reservation and operation hours (they closed weekends);

Higly recommend to visit this Community Center!

My friend brought me here the first time, and on my second visit alone, the staff was very friendly to me.
I bought:
Smoked salmon — rich and flavorful as always;
Thin sausages — tasty and not too fatty;
Strawberry jam — not what I expected (more like jelly or gummy strawberries), but still delicious;
Cheesecake — tastes great;
Eggplant & tomato spread for bread — haven’t tried it yet.

I’ll definitely come back again.

Halal!! Not sure what to make of this place; food was good; we had the Papadi chaat: not bad; the papas was a bit hard;  and there Saturday special: Chicken 65 Calupa: very tasty; the chalup is like a thick puri and the small mango cubes were a good touch

Atmosphere: very small tables and not enough for even 3 people; they also done do a good job of cleaning after someone leaves; it’s up to you to do it;
There is no service as you have to order on kiosk and menu is a bit confusing…
